From: Pad 2 bring-up <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: translate firmware BrickID type

The SM8350-style firmware ABI encodes Apple/BrickID as 9. Adding the SPR
AVS types to enum power_supply_usb_type moved the kernel's BrickID value
to 11, so copying the wire value now reports an unsupported SPR AVS type.
On this tablet a reconnect can return 9 and every USB supply uevent then
fails with "driver reporting unavailable enum value 9", flooding the log.

Translate this fixed wire value to the kernel enum. The other firmware
USB types (0 through 8) still match. This changes reporting only.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -90,6 +90,9 @@
 #define USB_ADAP_TYPE			7
 #define USB_MOISTURE_DET_EN		8
 #define USB_MOISTURE_DET_STS		9
+
+/* Fixed firmware ABI, independent of enum power_supply_usb_type. */
+#define BATTMGR_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID	9
 
 #define BATTMGR_WLS_PROPERTY_GET	0x34
 #define BATTMGR_WLS_PROPERTY_SET	0x35
@@ -1913,6 +1916,8 @@
 			break;
 		case USB_ADAP_TYPE:
 			battmgr->usb.usb_type = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			if (battmgr->usb.usb_type == BATTMGR_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID)
+				battmgr->usb.usb_type = POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID;
 			break;
 		case OPLUS_USB_PPS_STATUS:
 			battmgr->pps_status = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
